## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant design under privacy, governance, and ops constraints typical at large platforms, plus data residency and cost visibility.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant feature stores and private endpoints for isolation
- Privacy-preserving cross-tenant aggregation (secure aggregation + DP-SGD)
- Canary rollout and multi-region deployment for safe updates
- Data provenance with BigQuery Data Catalog and lineage tracking
- Per-tenant cost controls and explicit rollback criteria
- Data residency considerations (EU vs US tenants)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: privacy-preserving cross-tenant gradient aggregation
function aggregateCrossTenantGradients(grads, epsilon, delta) {
  // clip per-example gradients, add Gaussian noise, sum and normalize
  const clipped = grads.map(g => clip(g, 1.0));
  const sum = clipped.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
  const noise = gaussianNoise(epsilon, delta, sum.length);
  return (sum + noise) / grads.length;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify strict tenant isolation across feature stores and endpoints?
- What metrics and rollback criteria would you define for a canary rollout in this setup?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a candidate's ability to design a compliant, language-agnostic text classification pipeline using Vertex AI, Dataflow, and Pub/Sub, with privacy safeguards and practical operational concerns.

## Key Concepts

- Dataflow-based redaction and translation for multilingual content
- End-to-end data lineage: storage of raw and processed text
- Weekly Vertex AI training with canary deployment
- Drift and latency monitoring with rollback strategy
- Practical cost considerations: storage, translation, training, and serving

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: dataflow-style transform for redaction/translation
function redactAndTranslate(record) {
  const redacted = redactPII(record.text);
  const translated = (record.language !== 'en') ? translate(redacted, 'en') : redacted;
  return { id: record.id, text_en: translated, raw: record.text };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate translation quality across languages in this setup?
- What changes would you make to handle sudden traffic spikes without violating privacy constraints?

